    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_04439d7a38f24709afaaf6aab7b5d1adc8eb7efd5ed894ee583a31240433c8fa",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Weil cohomology turns cycles and products into graded linear algebra; its diagonal-kernel calculation converts Frobenius fixed points into alternating traces, hence into a determinant expression for the zeta function. Closed-point arithmetic then gives integral coprime numerator and denominator, and duality gives the functional equation, but purity is the additional input that separates degrees, prevents cancellation, and upgrades these reduced factors to the full degreewise Weil package including W4.",
