      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For curves, the source first identifies Riemann-hypothesis weights with square-root control of extension-field point-count errors; graph-diagonal intersection then represents those counts as correspondence traces, while Hodge-index defect positivity on a curve product and Rosati positivity on the Jacobian provide two concrete positivity realizations that force the required point-count or spectral bound.",
