    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_805ec35957163b1ef7ac42c40aeff837ed5926997ce4ccc04dba84235e6b4172",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The complex Kahler argument separates predictable degree growth from a unitary residual action using Hard Lefschetz and Hodge-Riemann positivity. In finite characteristic, a Weil form abstracts exactly the needed positive-adjoint interface, and the standard conjectures would algebraize the Kunneth projectors, Lefschetz lowering operator, and primitive intersection positivity so that the resulting star pairing is a Weil form and the polarized-endomorphism norm identity forces Frobenius weights.",
