    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ffe7574c6affa7a09746df18da42a9f271c46566cd49dd0a2db61a4b3ef0a1e8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Deligne's route uses two distinct amplification stages. In a hypersurface family, big monodromy locates the poles of even tensor-power local systems, nonnegative trace powers permit Landau's theorem, and taking increasingly high roots removes the fixed analytic loss to give the exact middle weight. Separately, Kunneth self-powers turn a uniform half-unit middle-degree window for general varieties into exact weights, after which cohomological padding or duality propagates them to every degree; Lefschetz-pencil induction is what supplies that window.",
